{#  =====================================================================
    WHY US — the private-build argument.
    Custom page, path "why-us". Static markup + one <style>; the FAQ is the
    real dashboard FAQ component, rendered by the components_order loop at
    the bottom of this branch (drag it onto this page in the Visual Editor).
    Review count uses [data-zz-rc], synced sitewide by snippets/polish.njk.
    ===================================================================== #}

<div class="wu-page">
  <div class="wu-bg" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="wu-bg__grid"></div>
    <div class="wu-bg__beam wu-bg__beam--a"></div>
    <div class="wu-bg__beam wu-bg__beam--b"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="wu-wrap">

    <header class="wu-head wu-rise">
      <p class="wu-eyebrow">WHY ZAZA</p>
      <h1 class="wu-title">Private build.<br>Not a public one.</h1>
      <p class="wu-sub">Every cheat gets detected eventually. What decides <em>when</em> is how many people are running the same binary you are &mdash; and that is the one number we actually control.</p>
    </header>

    <!-- THE CORE ARGUMENT -->
    <section class="wu-versus wu-rise" style="--d:.08s">
      <div class="wu-vs wu-vs--bad">
        <p class="wu-vs__tag wu-vs__tag--bad">Public / free build</p>
        <p class="wu-vs__num">10,000<span>+</span></p>
        <p class="wu-vs__label">people running the same file</p>
        <div class="wu-bar"><span class="wu-bar__fill wu-bar__fill--bad"></span></div>
        <ul class="wu-vs__list">
          <li>Downloadable by anyone &mdash; including anti-cheat staff</li>
          <li>Reverse-engineered and signatured within days</li>
          <li>Detections land on the whole userbase at once</li>
          <li>Re-uploaded, cracked, and bundled with malware</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="wu-vs__mid" aria-hidden="true"><span>VS</span></div>

      <div class="wu-vs wu-vs--good">
        <p class="wu-vs__tag wu-vs__tag--good">Zaza private build</p>
        <p class="wu-vs__num">Capped<span>.</span></p>
        <p class="wu-vs__label">paid, slot-limited userbase</p>
        <div class="wu-bar"><span class="wu-bar__fill wu-bar__fill--good"></span></div>
        <ul class="wu-vs__list">
          <li>Paid gate &mdash; there is no free copy to sample</li>
          <li>No public mirrors, no cracked builds in circulation</li>
          <li>Small footprint means far less worth analysing</li>
          <li>Re-verified after Rust updates before it goes back up</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHY USER COUNT IS THE MULTIPLIER -->
    <section class="wu-card wu-rise" style="--d:.14s">
      <p class="wu-kicker">THE MECHANIC</p>
      <h2 class="wu-h2">Why user count <em>is</em> the detection risk</h2>
      <p class="wu-p wu-mb">Anti-cheat teams don&rsquo;t find cheats by magic. They need a sample, a reason to prioritise it, and enough flagged machines to make a ban wave worth running. Every one of those steps scales with how popular a build is.</p>
      <ol class="wu-list">
        <li><strong>Getting a sample is trivial.</strong> If anyone can download it, so can they. A free public build sits in an analyst&rsquo;s sandbox the week it launches. Ours costs money and ships per key.</li>
        <li><strong>Signatures get written for the biggest targets first.</strong> Limited staff, ranked queue. A build with thousands of users is worth the engineering hours; a small private one usually isn&rsquo;t.</li>
        <li><strong>Ban waves are batched.</strong> Detections get held back and fired in bulk for maximum damage. The bigger the pool, the bigger the wave &mdash; and the better the odds you&rsquo;re in it.</li>
        <li><strong>Every extra user is another leak.</strong> Streamers, resellers, clip-happy friends. Popularity leaks a build into exactly the places you don&rsquo;t want it.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="wu-note">None of this makes any cheat risk-free. It&rsquo;s about which side of the maths you sit on.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- TABLE -->
    <section class="wu-card wu-rise" style="--d:.2s">
      <p class="wu-kicker">SIDE BY SIDE</p>
      <h2 class="wu-h2">Public builds vs this one</h2>
      <div class="wu-tablewrap">
        <table class="wu-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">&nbsp;</th><th scope="col">Public / free cheat</th><th scope="col" class="wu-th--good">Zaza private</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Userbase</th><td>Unlimited, anonymous</td><td class="wu-td--good">Slot-capped, paid</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">How you get it</th><td>Free download, mirrors, forums</td><td class="wu-td--good">Licence key, instant on payment</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Sample availability</th><td>Public &mdash; anyone can grab it</td><td class="wu-td--good">Behind a paid gate</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Typical lifespan</th><td>Days to weeks</td><td class="wu-td--good">Maintained build, re-verified per update</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">After a game update</th><td>Whenever someone bothers</td><td class="wu-td--good">Taken offline, updated, put back up</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Downtime honesty</th><td>You find out by getting banned</td><td class="wu-td--good"><a href="{{ '/status' | shopUrl }}">Public status page</a></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Support</th><td>A dead forum thread</td><td class="wu-td--good">Direct ticket, usually under 10 minutes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Malware risk</th><td>High &mdash; re-uploads are trivial to poison</td><td class="wu-td--good">One source, one loader</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHAT PRIVATE MEANS -->
    <section class="wu-rise" style="--d:.26s">
      <p class="wu-kicker wu-kicker--center">IN PRACTICE</p>
      <h2 class="wu-h2 wu-h2--center">What &ldquo;private&rdquo; actually means here</h2>
      <div class="wu-grid">
        <div class="wu-mini">
          <span class="wu-mini__ico">&#128274;</span>
          <h3 class="wu-mini__t">Paid gate, on purpose</h3>
          <p class="wu-mini__p">There is no free tier and no trial build floating around. Paying is friction &mdash; and friction is exactly what keeps casual scrapers and analysts out.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="wu-mini">
          <span class="wu-mini__ico">&#127919;</span>
          <h3 class="wu-mini__t">Slots, not scale</h3>
          <p class="wu-mini__p">We&rsquo;d rather cap the userbase than chase volume. Growing past what a build can safely carry is exactly how private cheats turn into public ones.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="wu-mini">
          <span class="wu-mini__ico">&#128736;</span>
          <h3 class="wu-mini__t">Updated, not abandoned</h3>
          <p class="wu-mini__p">Rust patches break things. The build goes down, gets updated and gets re-verified before it goes back up &mdash; rather than staying live and burning keys.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="wu-mini">
          <span class="wu-mini__ico">&#128225;</span>
          <h3 class="wu-mini__t">Status you can check</h3>
          <p class="wu-mini__p">Undetected, updating or down &mdash; it&rsquo;s on the <a href="{{ '/status' | shopUrl }}">status page</a> before you load in, not after. Extended downtime gets added back to your key.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="wu-mini">
          <span class="wu-mini__ico">&#9889;</span>
          <h3 class="wu-mini__t">Instant delivery</h3>
          <p class="wu-mini__p">Keys are automatic the moment payment clears. No queue, no &ldquo;DM me on Discord&rdquo;, no waiting on a reseller to wake up.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="wu-mini">
          <span class="wu-mini__ico">&#128172;</span>
          <h3 class="wu-mini__t">Support that answers</h3>
          <p class="wu-mini__p">Open a ticket and a human replies &mdash; typically in under 10 minutes. Setup help, config questions, replacements.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PROOF -->
    <section class="wu-proof wu-rise" style="--d:.32s">
      <div class="wu-proof__item">
        <p class="wu-proof__n"><span data-zz-rc>100</span></p>
        <p class="wu-proof__l">verified reviews</p>
      </div>
      <div class="wu-proof__item">
        <p class="wu-proof__n">&lt;10m</p>
        <p class="wu-proof__l">typical support reply</p>
      </div>
      <div class="wu-proof__item">
        <p class="wu-proof__n">1</p>
        <p class="wu-proof__l">build, maintained properly</p>
      </div>
      <div class="wu-proof__item">
        <p class="wu-proof__n">24/7</p>
        <p class="wu-proof__l">public status page</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- HONESTY -->
    <section class="wu-card wu-card--warn wu-rise" style="--d:.38s">
      <h2 class="wu-h2 wu-h2--sm"><span class="wu-warn">!</span> What we don&rsquo;t claim</h2>
      <p class="wu-p">No cheat is permanently undetected, and anyone telling you otherwise is selling you something. What we do claim is narrower and checkable: the build stays private, it comes down when it needs work, the status page says so honestly, and extended downtime is added back to your key. Play smart &mdash; sensible settings on a private build beat rage settings on any build.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="wu-cta wu-rise" style="--d:.44s">
      <h2 class="wu-cta__t">Ready when you are</h2>
      <p class="wu-cta__p">One build, keys by duration, instant delivery.</p>
      <a class="wu-btn" href="{{ '/product/zaza-rust-private-cheat' | shopUrl }}">
        View the build
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
      <p class="wu-cta__f"><a href="{{ '/status' | shopUrl }}">Live status</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <a href="{{ '/feedback' | shopUrl }}">Read the reviews</a></p>
    </section>

    <p class="wu-faqlead wu-rise" style="--d:.5s">Still deciding? The questions we get asked most:</p>

  </div>
</div>

